WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.209
(xylophone notes)

00:00:02.209 --> 00:00:04.827
- [Narrator] This is Sylvester,

00:00:04.827 --> 00:00:08.494
a three-year-old Sulawesi
Tarictic Hornbill.

00:00:09.637 --> 00:00:12.096
Endemic to Sulawesi, Indonesia,

00:00:12.096 --> 00:00:16.263
its once plentiful population
is now rapidly declining.

00:00:17.294 --> 00:00:19.496
Sylvester is on the smaller side,

00:00:19.496 --> 00:00:22.214
at about a foot and a half.

00:00:22.214 --> 00:00:24.559
Hornbills in general are characterized

00:00:24.559 --> 00:00:26.892
by their long, curved bills.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:30.638
This specific species makes its home

00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:33.821
in the tropical lowlands,
swamps and forests

00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:36.581
of Sulawesi and nearby islands

00:00:36.581 --> 00:00:38.781
where it feeds mainly on fruit,

00:00:38.781 --> 00:00:40.486
with the occasional small animal.

00:00:40.486 --> 00:00:42.214
(plucked strings music)

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:44.087
But, destruction of these areas

00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:47.420
has caused a massive drop in population.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:52.206
That, along with being hunted
for food and the pet trade,

00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:56.039
has left this once common
bird harder to spot.

00:00:57.908 --> 00:01:01.305
This is the Sulawesi Tarictic Hornbill.

00:01:01.305 --> 00:01:05.974
(xylophone music slows to a stop)

00:01:05.974 --> 00:01:08.391
(chime note)

